-- title:
--   A normalized union bound with an intersected first term
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega$ be finite and let $A,B,C\subseteq\Omega$. Their normalized indicator means satisfy
--   $$
--   \mathbb E\,1_{A\cap(B\cup C)}\le\mathbb E\,1_{A\cap B}+\mathbb E\,1_C.
--   $$
--   The second term counts all of $C$, so no assumption that $C\subseteq A$ is needed. The identity uses the normalized finite-mean convention even when $\Omega$ is empty.
